---
smd: 1
title: GitHub alerts
summary: Pins how GitHub alerts and blockquotes that look like them read, so later releases are compared against it.
updated: 2026-10-15
---

## Each kind

> [!NOTE]
> Useful information that users should know, even when skimming content.

> [!TIP]
> Helpful advice for doing things better or more easily.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Key information users need to know to achieve their goal.

> [!WARNING]
> Urgent info that needs immediate user attention to avoid problems.

> [!CAUTION]
> Advises about risks or negative outcomes of certain actions.

## Any case

> [!note]
> A lowercase marker.

> [!Warning]
> A mixed-case marker.

## Longer bodies

> [!TIP]
>
> A blank quote line after the marker, then **two** paragraphs with :badge[Beta] and `code`.
>
> - a list item
> - [ ] an open task
>
> ```sh
> smd validate docs
> ```

> [!WARNING]
> The first line of the body,
lazily continued on a line without the marker.

## Inside a container

:::card Release
> [!CAUTION]
> An alert inside a card.
:::

## Blockquotes that are not alerts

> [!NOTE] Text on the same line as the marker.

> [!UNKNOWN]
> An unknown kind.

> [! NOTE]
> A space inside the brackets.

> The marker is not on the first line.
> [!NOTE]
> More text.

> [!NOTE]

- > [!NOTE]
  > Inside a list item.

> > [!NOTE]
> > Inside another blockquote.

> **Note:** a bold label.

[!NOTE] outside a blockquote.

```md
> [!NOTE]
> Inside fenced code.
```
